"node_id":"C_kwDOEFLz89oAKGQ0MjY1Nzc5ZWY4MWZiMDgzZmI5N2NjZjczZTViNzRlMzYwMWIyZjQ","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/git/commits/d4265779ef81fb083fb97ccf73e5b74e3601b2f4","html_url":"https://github.com/juanfont/headscale/commit/d4265779ef81fb083fb97ccf73e5b74e3601b2f4","author":{"name":"Kristoffer Dalby","email":"kradalby@kradalby.no","date":"2021-10-27T06:44:04Z"},"committer":{"name":"Kristoffer Dalby","email":"kradalby@kradalby.no","date":"2021-10-27T06:44:04Z"},"tree":{"sha":"fbed2cfbc34886ce54b3c5b77a6df57693cb470d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/git/trees/fbed2cfbc34886ce54b3c5b77a6df57693cb470d"},"message":"Check in generated code\n\nThis does not have to be reviewed, here is some reasoning:\n\nGo (and go mod) is designed for having code available and we need to\ncheck in the generated code to make sure it is \"go gettable\". If we dont\nwe give ourselves a headache trying to setup all the ci, tests etc to\ninstall and generate the code before it runs.\n\nBecause the code isnt there, the plugins needed to generate the code\nfail to install...\n\nI didnt find any good documentation for this, but there is this github\ncomment:\nhttps://github.com/golang/go/issues/34514#issuecomment-535406759","parents":[{"sha":"8f2ef6a57de373cdeb5fb2236dbfd233bb57a15f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/git/commits/8f2ef6a57de373cdeb5fb2236dbfd233bb57a15f","html_url":"https://github.com/juanfont/headscale/commit/8f2ef6a57de373cdeb5fb2236dbfd233bb57a15f"}],"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null},"event":"committed"},{"sha":"2d9271909526e0ccdef9a750e673e34e9b3c68e3","node_id":"C_kwDOEFLz89oAKDJkOTI3MTkwOTUyNmUwY2NkZWY5YTc1MGU2NzNlMzRlOWIzYzY4ZTM","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/git/commits/2d9271909526e0ccdef9a750e673e34e9b3c68e3","html_url":"https://github.com/juanfont/headscale/commit/2d9271909526e0ccdef9a750e673e34e9b3c68e3","au